================================================================================
HYDROCLIMATIC INTERPRETATION — AUTO-GENERATED (v2.0 corrected)
================================================================================

1. STANDARD MK — TYPE I ERROR INFLATION
   At φ=0.30, empirical Type I error = 0.1295 (substantially exceeds nominal α=0.05). Consistent with Hamed & Rao (1998).

2. MMK (HAMED & RAO 1998) — IMPROVED CONTROL
   Type I error reduced to 0.0363 at φ=0.30 via rank-based VIF correction (VIF clamped ≥1.0 per corrected implementation).

3. PW-MK — AUTOCORRELATION REMOVAL
   Empirical Type I error = 0.0456 at φ=0.30. Reduces series length by one; slope reported on original series.

4. TFPW-MK (YUE & WANG 2002) — TREND PRESERVATION
   Type I error = 0.1476 at φ=0.30. At φ=0.60: var_ratio=0.910 (TFPW) vs 0.159 (PW); trend_attenuation=0.997 (TFPW) vs 0.090 (PW).

5. BH-FDR CORRECTION
   Benjamini–Hochberg (1995) correction now correctly applied to multi-station p-value arrays in fdr_analysis(), yielding true FDR values — not raw FWER rates as in the previous implementation.

6. STATISTICAL POWER (φ=0.3, trend=1.0 mm yr⁻¹)
   MK:0.9951 | MMK:0.7360 | PW:0.4232 | TFPW:0.9944

7. RECOMMENDATIONS
   (a) Always test autocorrelation (ACF, LB, DW) prior to trend analysis.
   (b) MMK preferred for moderate autocorrelation (0.1 ≤ φ < 0.5).
   (c) TFPW-MK preferred when trend estimation is the primary objective.
   (d) Standard MK only when |φ| < 0.10 or LB p > 0.05.
   (e) BH-FDR correction mandatory for multi-station analyses.

